diate"><addressbook><name>NGK INSULATORS, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, TOMONORI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISOMURA MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURASATO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI TOMONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISOMURA, MANABU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURASATO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, TOMONORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for manufacturing a filter having a ceramic porous film as a separating film, which comprises the step of forming a film from a film-forming slurry (9) containing aggregate particles comprising ceramics on the surface of a porous substrate (1), characterized in that the slurry (9) comprises an organic polymer for enlarging interstices between the aggregate particles and that the pore diameter of the resultant ceramic porous film can be controlled by the weight ratio between the aggregate particles and the organic polymer. The method permits the manufacture of a porous film having a desired pore diameter, independently of particle diameters of aggregate particles employed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de fabrication d'un filtre comportant un film poreux céramique comme film de séparation. Le procédé comporte l'étape consistant à former un film, sur la surface d'un substrat poreux (1), à partir d'une pâte filmogène (9) qui contient des particules d'agrégat comprenant de la céramique. Le procédé est caractérisé par le fait que la pâte (9) contient un polymère organique agrandissant les interstices entre les particules d'agrégat, et qu'on peut régler le diamètre des pores du film poreux céramique obtenu au moyen du rapport en poids des particules d'agrégat et du polymère organique. Le procédé permet de fabriquer un film poreux présentant un diamètre de pores voulu, indépendamment des diamètres de particules des particules d'agrégat employées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>